{"title":"2018 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2b","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2018 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> represents a rectangular field. There are three flagpoles: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. Paul runs along the path <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/6/fe68ac3de642bf43bab0b8fc4fc96cb2bb6a293a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\to D \\to C \\to M \\to A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"192\" height=\"14\" />. Tyler runs along the path <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/9/2696f38503399e61f53d67422764517fa91edc78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\to P \\to Q \\to C \\to B \\to A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"228\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the total distance that Tyler runs?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Opposite sides of a rectangle are equal to each other, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/e/92ed21798b09665e5878b87ed792efdd13ee931d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = CD = 105 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"155\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/3/603a8ff67765a1ca992ef428256f5d305f24be13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = CB = 200 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"155\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>From the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/9/cc9bcb8e913286bedf71705124d739c66c27709a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PD + AP = AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"135\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/e/12e150c0de48de5c39056c8bbc2fe6c221194a0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DQ + QC = CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"18\" />, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/8/43871b0599b79a0020709009ecafd5d591698d56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PD + 140 = 200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"133\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/3/183e13038a62c0f9913a848298e87220cf89ff00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DQ + 60 = 105$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32ecb9ed8aeed63f10b43363c9c8beb73afcc439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PD = 200 - 140 = 60 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"194\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43b1ddce3e6e1258ca55a577d1465249e50a105c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DQ = 105 - 60 = 45 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"185\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We also see that triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/8/758551d26e46cf2e97378d307eb9b551e0832136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" /> is a right triangle because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a rectangle, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/c/8bc611b65d58319582b50143152cff32f4a05cd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle PDQ = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" />. This means we can use the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pythagorean theorem\">Pythagorean theorem</a> to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, giving:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c17e80f6f0b57f3b7cbc4f59d9445463be6fdba8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PD^{2} + DQ^{2} = PQ^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"159\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/a/85ae914342b743c0839b766a7c483a6bb101ab9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ^{2} = 60^{2} + 45^{2} = 3600 + 2025 = 5625$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"315\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79a2b1a8abd8f14462f91130be5ef7a10603c7f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/0/ba075a4eec8101dfbf181584eaf0fd2223c8ac88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ = \\sqrt{5625} = 75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>Alternatively, we could have noticed that the side lengths of the triangle would have to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times the side lengths of a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/1/af1a2cb4ff1720f169ddde1726c1a5a1ab816ae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3-4-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" /> right triangle because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/5/895c9eb05bbc06087bf4a920a9b7ba161b5598c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\times 15 = 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/2/ee2bff79888fc255e11e0f75c7ebac55e0058a60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times 15 = 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/0/d3011a88f15c5f362a208a580d07b6fe2def0725.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ = 5 \\times 15 = 75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Next, we can realize that the total distance that Tyler runs is just the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perimeter\" title=\"Perimeter\">perimeter</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/3/c13f8af40a92e2af819852fdda8b6838f707c0a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APQCB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>From the diagram, this would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/7/5f7c0ad1603a393f42cd6efdb2803eb180c19548.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP + PQ + QC + CB + BA = 140 + 75 + 60 + 200 + 105 = \\boxed{580 \\text{ m}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"547\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018005313\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.021 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.040 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 112/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1213/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5951/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.640      1 2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\n100.00%   14.640      1 -total\n 37.25%    5.454      1 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36938:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018005313 and revision id 285745. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}